  "worked_solution": "To map the entire region $\u0394$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(2v(u-1),\\,\\frac{1}{2}v(4-u)) \\\\  & =(2v(0-1),\\,\\frac{1}{2}v(4-0)) \\\\  & =(-2v,2v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=-2v,\\,y=2v,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=-2t,\\,y(t)=2t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(-2,2)$ and $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063756/assets/e6ef0f52fbe6638659dd7b7f3d702d4bfbb07b83a7f7742c9b0822157908b706.png)",
